insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('52e7118e-7e36-59b0-a057-593ba36dd24d', 'rg4-evidence-inference-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-evidence-inference'), null,
        '3-5', $q$How a Hot Air Balloon Flies$q$, $q$A hot air balloon has three main parts. There is a giant cloth bag called the envelope. There is a basket where people stand. Between them is a burner that makes a big flame.

The balloon flies because hot air is lighter than cool air. When the pilot turns on the burner, the air inside the envelope gets hot. The hot air pushes the balloon up into the sky. To come down, the pilot lets the air cool off. The balloon then sinks slowly toward the ground.

A pilot cannot steer a balloon the way a driver steers a car. There is no wheel and no motor to push it sideways. Instead, the pilot moves the balloon up or down to find winds blowing in different directions. A wind near the ground might blow east, while a wind higher up might blow north.

Most balloon flights take place early in the morning or near sunset. At those times, the winds are usually calm and gentle. A crew on the ground follows the balloon in a truck. When the balloon lands, the crew helps fold the envelope and pack everything away.$q$, 'draft')
