insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ce3bd806-2863-5b11-aed8-12e10154e5d7', 'rg4-evidence-inference-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-evidence-inference'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Riders of the Mail Trail$q$, $q$Long ago, sending a letter across the western United States could take weeks. In 1860, a company started a fast mail service with riders on horseback. People called it the Pony Express.

The trail stretched nearly two thousand miles. Small stations stood along the way. At each station, a rider jumped onto a fresh horse and kept going. Tired horses could not run fast, so the switch saved a lot of time. After many hours, a rider handed the mail bag to the next rider.

The riders had to travel light. They carried the mail in a leather cover that fit over the saddle. Letters were written on very thin paper to keep the load small. Sending one letter cost a lot of money, so most people could not afford it.

With this system, mail crossed the trail in about ten days. That was much faster than before. But the Pony Express lasted only about a year and a half. In 1861, workers finished a telegraph line across the country. Now messages could travel by wire in minutes. The riders were no longer needed.$q$, 'draft')
