   $q$In paragraph 2, the clay "flopped over like a sleepy puppy." What does this simile show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The clay stood up tall and stayed very straight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The clay made a soft snoring sound on the wheel.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The clay drooped and fell over in a soft heap.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The clay turned into the shape of a little dog.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The clay drooped and fell over in a soft heap.$q$, $q$A sleepy puppy flops down limply, so the simile shows the clay sagging and falling. Mia says "I ruined it," which proves the clay did not stand up or become a dog shape.$q$, 'draft', 'dd336eed-36a2-5926-b347-1e1ed06c54c6')
