   $q$In paragraph 5, Mia held her hands "as still as stones." What does this simile mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She moved her hands quickly back and forth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She kept her hands from moving at all.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She held real stones in both of her hands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She made her hands very cold and gray.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She kept her hands from moving at all.$q$, $q$Stones do not move, so the simile shows Mia kept her hands perfectly steady. Because her hands stayed still, the clay "rose up" instead of flopping over.$q$, 'draft', 'dd336eed-36a2-5926-b347-1e1ed06c54c6')
