   $q$In paragraph 3, "The riders had to be light, brave, and tough." Which word is the best synonym for "tough" as it is used here?$q$, $q$[{"text":"chewy","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning-of-multiple-meaning-word"},{"text":"sturdy","is_correct":true},{"text":"weak","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"antonym-for-synonym"},{"text":"difficult","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning-of-multiple-meaning-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$sturdy$q$, $q$The riders faced deserts, mountains, and bad weather, so "tough" means strong and able to handle hard things, like "sturdy." "Difficult" is another meaning of tough, but it describes a problem, not a person.$q$, 'draft', 'f3ea092c-b68e-571f-87b8-285b2ed6a410')
