-- Passage rg4-main-idea-summary-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('7255f4ca-fd65-5068-900b-672e3e76ff68', 'rg4-main-idea-summary-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-main-idea-summary'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Sea Otters Protect the Kelp Forest$q$, $q$Along some rocky coasts, tall seaweed called kelp grows in thick underwater forests. Fish hide among its long leaves. Crabs, snails, and seals live there too. A small, furry animal helps keep this forest healthy: the sea otter.

Sea otters eat many kinds of sea animals, but one favorite is the sea urchin. A sea urchin is a round, spiny creature that crawls along the sea floor. Urchins eat kelp. They chew through the bottom of the plant, and then the whole plant floats away.

When there are plenty of otters, they eat lots of urchins. The number of urchins stays small, so the kelp can grow tall. When otters disappear from an area, urchins can spread quickly. In a few years, they may eat a whole kelp forest down to bare rock.

Scientists have seen this happen. In some places, otters became rare, and the kelp vanished. Later, when otters returned, the kelp forests grew back. Fish and other animals came back as well.

This shows how one animal can matter to a whole community of living things. By eating urchins, sea otters help protect a home for hundreds of other creatures.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
