-- Passage rg4-text-structure-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('814bbb48-1c10-56de-9ddf-22ab2d6ce631', 'rg4-text-structure-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Why the River Rises in Spring$q$, $q$Every spring, the Pine River near the town of Marlow gets wider and faster. Sometimes it even spills over its banks. What causes this to happen?

The main cause is melting snow. All winter, snow piles up on the hills around the river. When the weather warms up in spring, the snow melts. The water runs down the hills and into the river.

Spring rain adds even more water. The ground is still cold and hard, so the rain cannot soak in. Instead, it flows straight into the river.

Because of all this extra water, the river rises quickly. Low roads near the water can be covered. The town closes these roads until the water goes down.

The high water also brings some good effects. It carries rich soil onto nearby fields. As a result, farmers often grow strong crops there in summer.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
