-- Passage rg4-text-structure-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ed7a39ed-9898-557a-833d-b8a0dc2d25ae', 'rg4-text-structure-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Better Food for the Ducks$q$, $q$Families in the town of Brookfield love to visit Willow Pond. For years, many visitors tossed bread to the ducks. The ducks seemed happy, but the bread was causing a problem.

Bread fills ducks up, but it does not give them what they need to stay healthy. Ducks that eat too much bread can grow weak. Also, bread that the ducks did not eat sank and rotted. It made the water cloudy and smelly.

A group of fourth graders at Brookfield Elementary decided to help. First, they made signs explaining why bread is bad for ducks. Next, they asked the park to sell small cups of duck food made from grains and seeds. The money from the cups would help pay for park cleanups.

The plan worked. Visitors still enjoy feeding the ducks, but now they use healthy food. Within a year, the pond water was clearer, and the ducks looked stronger.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
