   $q$Which lines from the poem state the theme most directly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"The kite began to rise and climb, / up past the oak, one tug at a time.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"event-not-theme"},{"text":"\"I ran and yanked it, hard and fast. / It flipped and flopped and fell at last.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"\"Sometimes the way to help things soar / is holding on a little less, not more.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"My kite lay flat upon the ground, / a paper bird that made no sound.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"describes-setting"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Sometimes the way to help things soar / is holding on a little less, not more."$q$, $q$The last two lines move from the kite to a lesson about life. The lines about the kite rising tell what happened, but they do not state the lesson.$q$, 'draft', '60380577-c54a-532a-8e39-a499db1f8741')
