   $q$Which sentence best states the theme of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Young people should do hard tasks for adults to save time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-of-theme"},{"text":"With patience, anyone can be both a teacher and a learner.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Chess is a more useful skill than making video calls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Tablets are too hard for older people to ever learn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$With patience, anyone can be both a teacher and a learner.$q$, $q$Theo patiently teaches Pop Eli, and then Pop Eli patiently teaches Theo. Pop Eli does learn to make the call, so the choice that says tablets are too hard for older people goes against the story.$q$, 'draft', '512e5387-f430-5156-a9d8-0dc70dbb0ce5')
